rs worldwide  volume 2 improved on its predecessor's  worldwide box office gross and cemented  that these characters were no one movie  flukes even with a new version of groot  on the team  the adorable baby groot still voiced by  diesel was everywhere on toys posters  and tv spots for guardians of the galaxy  vol 2  capturing the hearts of moviegoers  before the movie even opened diesel's  baby groot helped to promise moviegoers  that they wouldn't just be getting the  first guardians again with this new  sequel  it's no wonder then that guardians of  the galaxy vol 2 scored so much success  at the box office that it became  diesel's biggest non-fast and furious  movie of all time  with the 2017 entry the fate of the  furious a furious movie made less than  its predecessor for the first time since  tokyo drift in 2006.  although not an ideal turn of events it  was inevitable given that this film was  following up on furious 7 which had  taken the franchise to new  astronomical box office heights it was  unreasonable to expect vin diesel's  signature franchise to keep topping  itself worldwide but fate still managed  to do just fine on its own merits  grossing 1.2 billion dollars worldwide  the fate of the furious was the second  biggest entry in the franchise by a  massive margin  though diesel's furious movies were no  longer consistently one-upping each  other in terms of box office halls  fate showed that this series could still  easily shift things into high gear and  deliver impressive box office numbers  though it was the seventh entry in the  furious saga furious 7 was far from a  routine movie in the franchise  for one thing this was the first entry  in the series since too fast too furious  to not be directed by justin lin with  james juan instead sitting in the  director's chair  even more notably though this would be  the last furious title to feature paul  walker's brian o'connor  after walker's tragic death in a car  accident in november 2013 the film 